    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1650">

                <pb facs="1047" n="931" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg931"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 511.4A1/1481.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Delegate Van Dyke to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 22. We are confident adjournment to a definite date this summer would
                    not be accepted by the Conference nor tend to promote unanimity. Turkey is
                    immovable. The Netherlands Government declined to approach Turkey again. A
                    disposition to put into effect the Convention now, is strong among certain
                    powers including all American, principal Asiatic powers, Netherlands, Belgium
                    and probably others—in our opinion a forward step and the best way to ultimately
                    bring in the other nations. Otherwise we think the Conference will adjourn
                    without date and thus lose the advance made. Netherlands Delegation will propose
                    to put into effect the Convention by a group of powers. Will you consent? If
                    conditionally, state conditions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Dyke</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
